details:
(a) the key objectives and major reforms proposed under the Electricity (Amendment) Rules, 2026 and the Draft National Electricity Policy, 2026;
(b) the manner in which these reforms are expected to improve the financial sustainability of the power sector, enhance operational efficiency and ensure reliable, round-the-clock electricity supply to consumers; and
(c) the steps taken to consult State Governments and other stakeholders before finalising these reforms and to facilitate their effective implementation across the country?

(a) the number of Central sector infrastructure projects currently being monitored in the State of Telangana;
(b) the number of such projects in the State facing cost or time overruns as on date;
(c) the total approved cost versus the latest anticipated cost of these projects in the State; and
(d) the steps taken by Government to improve project implementation monitoring and reduce delays nationally?

(a) the initiatives taken by Government to promote GI-tagged handloom products of Telangana, including Pochampally Ikat, Gadwal Sarees, Narayanpet Sarees and Warangal Durries, in domestic and international markets;
(b) whether Government proposes to leverage emerging export opportunities under India's trade agreements to enhance global market access for GI-tagged handloom products;
(c) whether any exhibitions, buyer-seller meets, handloom expos are being planned for promoting Telangana's handloom products; and
(d) the steps taken to provide direct-to-buyer market access to Telangana weavers through the India Handloom Brand and GeM portal?

(a) the progress made in promoting tribal homestay tourism under Swadesh Darshan 2.0 and other tourism initiatives, including in Telangana and other tribal regions;
(b) the initiatives taken to position India as a global hub for medical tourism, including leveraging world-class healthcare centres such as Hyderabad and to strengthen the skills of tourism stakeholders, tourist guides and hospitality workers; and
(c) the measures being taken to develop MICE tourism infrastructure, including convention centres, to promote business and conference tourism across the country?

(a) the progress made under Pradhan Mantri Matsya Sampada Yojana (PMMSY) in Telangana, including the assistance sanctioned and the major activities supported under the scheme;
(b) the measures taken to strengthen cold chain infrastructure, fish markets and fish processing facilities, particularly in inland districts of the State; and
(c) the role of the National Fisheries Development Board (NFDB), headquartered in Hyderabad, in implementing PMMSY and supporting small and marginal fish farmers through technology, training and market linkages?

(a) the criteria for selecting locations for the 5 Integrated Medical Hubs announced in Budget 2026-27 and whether Hyderabad, a major centre for healthcare, pharma and medical technology is being considered;
(b) the regulatory and infrastructure framework being designed to attract private sector investment into these hubs, including the PPP model envisaged; and
(c) the steps taken to further boost medical tourism, given that India received over 6 lakh medical tourists in 2024 and the role of simplified visa and health corridor policies?

(a) the progress made under Pradhan Mantri Ayushman Bharat Health Infrastructure Mission (PM-ABHIM) in strengthening public health infrastructure;
(b) the measures being taken to assist States in timely implementation of approved projects and optimal utilisation of funds under PM-ABHIM;
(c) whether Government proposes to expand specialized healthcare services, advanced facilities and research capabilities at AIIMS Bibinagar to meet the growing healthcare needs of the region; and
(d) the measures being taken to enhance AIIMS Bibinagar role in healthcare delivery in Telangana and neighbouring States?

(a) whether the Income Tax Department has undertaken any campaign to help taxpayers transition from the Income Tax Act, 1961 to the Income Tax Act, 2025;
(b) if so, the details thereof;
(c) the number of cases withdrawn, not filed or otherwise impacted due to the revised monetary limits, forum-wise and tax-wise, along with the estimated reduction in litigation burden and tax demand locked in disputes; and
(d) whether the CBDT has undertaken any measures to ease compliance for taxpayers during the last five years, if so, the details thereof?

(a) the status of MSME registrations on the Udyam Portal in the State of Telangana and the employment opportunities created thereby;
(b) the initiatives taken to facilitate the participation of MSMEs from Telangana in the Production Linked Incentive (PLI) Schemes and the benefits accruing to them; and
(c) the measures being taken to strengthen MSME clusters in key sectors such as pharmaceuticals and textiles in the State, including support for technology, infrastructure and market access?

(a) the initiatives being undertaken to strengthen Telangana's role as a leading palm oil producing State under the National Mission on Edible Oils–Oil Palm (NMEO-OP);
(b) the measures taken to support integrated palm oil value chains through expansion of processing facilities, logistics and market linkages, especially in Telangana; and
(c) the steps being taken to promote sustainable cultivation, intercropping and adoption of modern technologies for enhancing farmers' income while contributing to India's edible oil self-reliance?

(a) the current status of Bhongir Fort Experiential Zone project under Swadesh Darshan 2.0 in Yadadri-Bhuvanagiri;
(b) the strategy adopted to promote lesser-known tourism destinations in Telangana under Swadesh Darshan 2.0;
(c) the broad outcomes envisaged under the Scheme in promoting sustainable, heritage and experience-based tourism across the country; and
(d) the measures taken to ensure participation of local communities, artisans and MSMEs in the planning and implementation of projects under the scheme?

(a) the steps taken following inclusion of Mudumal Megalithic Menhirs in Telangana on India's UNESCO Tentative World Heritage List in March 2025;
(b) the steps taken for archaeological documentation, scientific conservation, site management, community participation and visitor infrastructure at the site; and
(c) the broader strategy of Government for increasing India's tally of UNESCO World Heritage Sites beyond the current 44?

(a) the progress of the northern corridor of the Hyderabad Regional Ring Road (RRR) under Bharatmala Pariyojana Phase I, including the percentage of land acquired, length of road constructed, and the latest completion timeline;
(b) the status of the Central Government's approval on the revised project cost and the timeline for environmental and forest clearances to the southern corridor; and
(c) the number of National Highway stretches from Telangana included under PPP models, and the anticipated capital receipts from these transactions and their reinvestment into new road projects in the State?

(a) the salient reforms introduced under the Insolvency and Bankruptcy Code (Amendment) Act, 2026 to strengthen the insolvency resolution framework and improve ease of doing business;
(b) the manner in which these reforms are expected to reduce resolution timelines and improve creditor recovery; and
(c) the steps taken to operationalise the provisions relating to group insolvency and cross-border insolvency, including the institutional and regulatory framework envisaged for their effective implementation?

(a) the progress made in implementation of the Viability Gap Funding scheme for Battery Energy Storage Systems (BESS), including the storage capacity awarded and commissioned; 
(b) the measures taken to promote deployment of standalone and co-located battery storage projects for renewable energy integration, improve grid flexibility and enhance power reliability; 
(c) the role envisaged for BESS in meeting peak electricity demand and supporting grid reliability; and, 
(d) whether Government proposes additional policy regulatory or financial measures to accelerate the adoptive of energy storage technologies across the country; and
(e) if so, the details thereof?

(a) the number of Eklavya Model Residential Schools (EMRS) sanctioned, operational and under construction and the steps taken to address teacher vacancies in EMRS across the State of Telangana;
(b) the academic outcomes including Board examination results, higher education enrolment rate of EMRS alumni and any sports or skill achievements of EMRS students from Telangana in the last three years; and
(c) the steps for preservation of tribal culture, language and traditional knowledge through education initiatives?

(a) the steps taken to ensure accessibility and reasonable accommodation for Persons with Disabilities (PwDs) in public recruitment and competitive examinations;
(b) whether Government has issued revised guidelines on the provision of scribes, assistive technologies and examination accommodations;
(c) the measures taken to ensure uniform implementation of these guidelines by recruiting agencies and examination authorities; and
(d) the mechanism in place to monitor compliance, address grievances and safeguard the rights of candidates with disabilities during the recruitment process?

(a) whether the Ministry has reviewed the implementation of the ‘National Road Safety Strategy and Action Plan’ during 2026;
(b) if so, the details thereof;
(c) whether financial assistance has been released to the States and Union Territories for rectification of ‘black spots’ and other road safety-related measures during the last two years; and
(d) if so, the details thereof?

(a) the progress made under the National Green Hydrogen Mission, including the implementation status of the Strategic Interventions for Green Hydrogen Transition (SIGHT) Programme;
(b) the details of incentives extended for green hydrogen production, electrolyser manufacturing, energy storage technologies and the extent of private sector participation;
(c) the measures taken to position India as a global hub for green hydrogen production and exports; and
(d) whether Government proposes to extend green hydrogen-linked industrial incentives to Telangana's chemical and fertilizer sectors, and if so, the details thereof?

(a) the status of the single-dose HPV vaccination programme launched on 28 February 2026 for girls aged 14 years;
(b) the vaccination coverage targets under the programme and the institutional mechanism being utilised for delivery and whether WHO targets for elimination of cervical cancer would be met; 
(c) the steps taken to address vaccine hesitancy and ensure high uptake among girls in rural, tribal, and urban slum areas; and
(d) Government's broader strategy to reduce cervical cancer incidence and mortality in the country, including screening programmes linked to the HPV vaccination drive and awareness campaigns across States and Union Territories?

(a) the outcomes of the expansion of the Pradhan Mantri Garib Kalyan Anna Yojana (PMGKAY) since January 2025; 
(b) whether the Government has conducted any assessment or evaluation of the effectiveness or impact of the scheme in providing support to vulnerable sections during economic challenges; 
(c) if so, the details thereof; and 
(d) the future action plan regarding this scheme, including proposed amendments, technical improvements, or convergence with other welfare schemes, and the details thereof?

(a) the details of fertilizer units that remained closed prior to 2014 and have been revived by Government thereafter, unit-wise; 
(b) the annual production capacity added through the revival of the Ramagundam, Gorakhpur, Sindri, Barauni and Talcher plants after 2014;
(c) the total investment made and employment generated through these revived units;
(d) whether any such closed units were revived during the period prior to 2014; and
(e) the reasons for which these units could not be revived earlier and the manner in which they have been made operational after 2014?

(a) the steps taken for mainstreaming and integration of AYUSH systems into the national healthcare framework including co-location in health and wellness centres; 
(b) the progress achieved in research, standardisation, quality control and pharmacovigilance of AYUSH medicines; 
(c) the impact of AYUSH interventions on preventive healthcare, wellness and management of lifestyle diseases; and
(d) the future plans to further strengthen AYUSH education, infrastructure and its contribution towards holistic healthcare in line with Viksit Bharat @2047?

(a) the steps taken by the Central Government to facilitate an equitable resolution of the inter-State water-sharing issues relating to the Krishna and Godavari river basins between the States of Telangana and Andhra Pradesh;
(b) the progress made by the recently constituted 13-member committee, including its terms of reference, key recommendations, if any and the expected timeline for submission of its report; and
(c) the assistance and coordination being provided by the Centre to ensure timely implementation of the Committee's recommendations and a lasting resolution of the disputes?

(a) the status of metro rail projects sanctioned and under implementation across the country, including project-wise physical progress as on June, 2026;
(b) the details of central financial assistance provided for metro rail projects;
(c) whether any new metro rail projects or corridors, including Hyderabad Metro Rail Phase-II, have been approved or are under consideration and, if so, the present status thereof; and
(d) the measures taken to improve urban mobility, last-mile connectivity and reduce traffic congestion through metro rail expansion?

(a) whether Government has taken steps to promote coal gasification and other cleaner coal technologies during 2026 including the State of Bihar;
(b) the number of coal gasification projects approved or under implementation, and their current status;
(c) whether any financial incentives or viability gap funding mechanisms have been introduced to support such projects, if so, the details thereof; and
(d) the expected improvement in coal utilisation efficiency and reduction in emissions and enhancing domestic energy security through these technologies?

(a) the details of progress made in developing integrated tourist circuits with world-class infrastructure at key spiritual and cultural destinations;
(b) the specific projects and amenities developed in Telangana, within the Hyderabad Heritage circuit and their role in enhancing visitor experience;
(c) how this infrastructure-led approach is boosting domestic tourism, creating local employment and promoting regional arts, crafts and cuisine; and
(d) the details of strategy adopted to market these destinations effectively to both the domestic and international tourists?

(a) the historic outcomes and global consensus particularly on critical issues like digital public infrastructure, green development, climate finance and reformed multilateralism;
(b) how the 'Voice of the Global South' summit centred the developmental priorities and concerns of developing nations in the international discourse, establishing a new model for inclusive diplomacy;
(c) the long-term strategic, economic and diplomatic benefits for India's global standing arising from this successful leadership of the premier global forum; and
(d) the steps being taken to consolidate and build upon these gains in India's ongoing bilateral and multilateral engagements?

(a) the number of students admitted under the Scheme for Residential Education for Students in High Schools in Targeted Areas (SHRESHTA) since its revision for the period 2023–24 to 2025–26, along with the number of participating schools across States/UTs;
(b) the details of modalities adopted for selection of students through the National Entrance Test for SHRESHTA (NETS) and the mechanism for allocation of seats in residential schools; and
(c) the financial assistance provided under the scheme towards tuition, hostel facilities and other support services for students admitted in classes IX and XI?

(a) whether the Directorate General of Training (DGT) successfully signed a Flexi-MoU with Bajaj Auto on 6th March, 2026, and other private companies for advanced manufacturing;
(b) if so, the details thereof;
(c) how will the Industry-Integrated Skilling Model provide youth with hands-on training in high-tech automotive manufacturing;
(d) what specific role does the ‘Badhna Hai Toh Yahan Judna Hai’ campaign play in promoting these vocational courses; and
(e) how many youth have successfully enrolled in Aeronautics programmes at the new India-France Excellence Centre in Kanpur?

(a) the number of Automated Permanent Academic Account Registry (APAAR) IDs successfully generated for students as of March, 2026;
(b) how the integration of APAAR with DigiLocker has improved the seamless transfer of academic credits between institutions;
(c) what specific measures ensure parental consent and data privacy during the 12-digit student ID registration process;
(d) whether the Ministry has successfully made APAAR IDs mandatory for appearing in the 2026 Board Examinations; 
(e) if so, the details thereof; and 
(f) how many schools have updated student demographic details on the Unified District Information System for Education (UDISE+) portal to facilitate error-free ID creation?

(a) the details of central assistance provided under the Pradhan Mantri Krishi Sinchayee Yojana (PMKSY) for the completion of ongoing major and medium irrigation projects and micro-irrigation in the State of Telangana during the last three years;
(b) the technical and financial support extended by the Central Water Commission (CWC) for the review and optimisation of large projects like the Kaleshwaram Lift Irrigation Project; and
(c) the expected impact of these irrigation projects on agricultural productivity, farmer incomes and drought-proofing in the State of Telangana?

(a) the steps taken to ensure quality and quantity of fuel at retail outlets in the State of Telangana through regular inspections and technology integration;
(b) whether Government has introduced any digital initiatives (e.g., fuel home delivery, digital payments) to enhance consumer convenience; and
(c) the plans to upgrade fuel stations with EV charging facilities and multi-fuel options along major highways across the nation, particularly in the State of Telangana?

(a) the progress of City Gas Distribution (CGD) network expansion in the State of Telangana, particularly in Hyderabad and other major cities and the number of PNG (piped natural gas) connections and CNG stations operational;
(b) the steps taken to ensure last-mile connectivity to households and industries in newly authorised geographical areas (GAs), especially in the State under recent bidding rounds;
(c) whether Government has assessed the environmental and economic benefits of switching to natural gas in the State transport and industrial sectors; and
(d) the timeline for completing the natural gas grid and pipeline infrastructure to cover all districts of the State?
